docs {
  # Update Watch Progress

  Upserts playback progress for a movie or TV episode (`POST /api/watch-history/update-progress`).
  Requires authentication (`authMiddleware`).
  - Conflict resolution is keyed on `(profileId, tmdbId, mediaType, seasonNumber, episodeNumber)`.
  - For movies, `seasonNumber` and `episodeNumber` default to `0` if omitted.
  - A title is automatically marked `completed = true` when `progressSeconds >= durationSeconds * 0.9`.

  ## Request Body
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `tmdbId` | `number` | Yes | Numeric TMDB identifier. |
  | `mediaType` | `"movie" \| "tv"` | Yes | Content media type. |
  | `progressSeconds` | `number` | Yes | Playback position in seconds. |
  | `durationSeconds` | `number` | Yes | Total duration in seconds. |
  | `title` | `string` | No | Display title of the content. |
  | `posterPath` | `string` | No | Relative TMDB poster path. |
  | `playbackId` | `string` | No | Mux playback ID (`muxPlaybackId`). |
  | `seasonNumber` | `number` | No | Season number (`0` for movies). |
  | `episodeNumber` | `number` | No | Episode number (`0` for movies). |

  ## Responses
  - **200 OK**: `{ "success": true }`.
  - **401 Unauthorized**: `{ "error": "Unauthorized" }`.
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
}

